 monitor the ones you are  using right now and see your account  information with data and research  projects you are working on the  pipeline's crunching big data do not  require even a single line of code the  platform allows for large scale analysis  from a web interface that anyone can  learn to use as a result researchers can  fully integrate analysis into their  research taking sample data and  integrating it with repositories that  they have collected and already trust  the pipeline builder remains flexible  offering intuitive suggestions and  enriching the process with informative  pop-ups and assisting with reproducible  research at the file data and visual  levels the front-end pipelines can be  easily monitored and edited by an expert  that can deploy a redundant tasks at  scale leveraging efficient big data  processing capabilities behind the  scenes the analytical capacity of the  t-bone 4 platform allows the users to  work with sequence structure and  molecules at the bulk or even single  cell level discovering complex  relationships by following a logical  transition from single to multi-omics  data where genomics epigenomics  metagenomics proteomics and metabolomics  can be analyzed to reveal a systems  biology view of phenotype genotype  relationships spanning diverse and  heterogeneous data sources from patient  derived cell lines to xenograft models  and clinical trials the platform vision  originated from dr. Lena Brodsky who has  extensive academic and commercial  experience with both biostatistics and  bioinformatics behind the vision there  is an experienced team that is working  on  aspects of the platform  commercialization and growth and  expansion to address research questions  that are being solved by cutting-edge  researchers around the world the company  is based at the bio Innovation Center in  New Orleans and is working closely with  a number of collaborators from various  US and international institutions
 

